All tests passed. Here's what I implemented:

**`transpose.py`** — A `transpose(text)` function that:
1. Splits the input text into lines
2. Finds the maximum line length
3. For each column index, builds a new row by collecting characters from each original line at that index, padding with spaces where a line is too short
4. Strips trailing spaces from each transposed row (no padding to the right)
5. Joins the result rows with newlines

This handles all the specified cases: equal-length inputs, unequal-length inputs with left-padding, and empty input.
